<title>UK: UK CBI Jan monthly trends survey - table.</title>
<headline>UK CBI Jan monthly trends survey - table.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Here are tabulated results from the January monthly survey of trends in UK manufacturing by employers group Confederation of British Industry (CBI).</p>
<p> CBI MONTHLY TRENDS ENQUIRY (a)   Jan,97  Dec,96  Nov,96  Oct,96</p>
<p> - total order book		    -6     -10	 0     -9</p>
<p> - export order book		   -8     -15	 -5    -7</p>
<p> - stocks of finished goods	 +20     +17     +15     +18</p>
<p> - output expectations *	    +14     +13     +21     +20</p>
<p> - domestic price expectations *  +16     +12	+8	+7</p>
<p>NOTES - * over the coming four months;</p>
<p>	 - (a) in pct, giving balance between those replying &quot;up',</p>
<p>&quot;above normal' or &quot;more than adequate,' and those replying &quot;down', &quot;below normal' or &quot;less than adequate.'</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 71 542 7715</p>
</text>
